WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.940
KARNO TENOVUO: The mission
is to make autonomous

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.470
ships a commercial reality.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.950
When we originally
set out to do that,

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:19.170
we thought that it would
happen a bit later, 2025-ish.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.390
Now we see that the market
disruption is actually

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.940
happening much faster.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.830
And we need to take into
account many activities.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.340
So we start from the
intelligent awareness,

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.920
basically giving the
ice to the vessel.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.790
We are also working on
connectivity solutions,

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:40.230
so transforming the data
from ships to shore.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.410
We're building remote
operations centers.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.450
So basically the
infrastructure that you

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.600
need in order to operate
vessels from shoreside

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.980
and monitor them.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.770
And then we are developing
autonomous systems

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.480
starting from
navigation systems,

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.600
but also, then, later on
moving into machinery systems,

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.470
so basically covering the
whole vessel that will

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:06.170
be made autonomous one by one.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.170
We're looking to basically
automate the data flow

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:13.630
from censoring to data
warehousing to annotation,

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:17.750
and then to machine learning
models and training the models.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.910
And we're looking to
automate that data flow,

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:27.390
and really, Google is the
best partner for that.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:34.000
Autonomous ships will affect,
basically, safety, reliability,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.130
and efficiency.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:38.380
Those are the three main
drivers, safety, reliability,

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.750
and efficiency.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:43.830
That is basically driving
the whole development.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.440
On the safety
side, you will have

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.380
a lot of accidents that
are happening today

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.470
are happening for the
crew on board the vessels.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.740
And now we can save
a lot of accidents

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.040
from happening when we are
actually moving the work

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.220
to shoreside, or
then making that work

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.136
more automated in the future.

00:02:04.136 --> 00:02:05.010
So that is one thing.

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:08.759
And of course, reliability
comes, that there's

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:10.380
a lot of breakdowns today.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.810
The systems onboard the
vessels are not reliable.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:17.700
So they have to do a lot of
maintenance while in operation

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.810
today.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:22.360
In the future, when the
systems are more autonomous,

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:26.560
they also need to be more
reliable so there isn't

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.550
so much need for the
kind of maintenance work

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.040
that you have on board
the vessels today.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.620
And then on the efficiency
side, you can, of course,

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.220
now have the same team
of experts sitting

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.570
in a good office environment
supporting multiple ships

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:46.930
or tens of ships instead of
having technical expertise

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.390
in each of the ships.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:54.830
So the work is the same
but now more efficient.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:58.190
We can already use a lot
of the solutions that

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:00.980
have been created for other
industries in the machine

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:05.740
learning space, and we can
now apply them to change

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.890
the shipping world as well.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.810
There is a lot of things
we haven't done yet.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.860
So we need to, for
example, create now

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:15.410
the machine learning models
and train them for marine use.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:18.820
We need to basically
gather the data

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:23.510
so that we can train the models,
also, for example in nighttime

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:28.460
and in different
weather conditions

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:31.420
and different viewing angles.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.310
That kind of data set we need to
create so we can have the best

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:37.250
models out there.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.950
In ships you have a
wider area to cover.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:45.440
We're using LIDAR, we're
using radar, HD cameras.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.470
We have to cover a
wide area because there

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:52.910
can be very unpredicted
movements of a lot of vessels.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:56.810
That requires a high computing
power on board the vessel.

00:03:56.810 --> 00:04:00.470
And the good thing is that
they have a bit more time

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:03.560
to do the analysis, for
example, compared to cars.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.140
Some of the Google Cloud
technologies we're using

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.840
include, for example,
TensorFlow processing unit

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.180
that we can have on
board the vessels.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.910
You have data jobs.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:20.600
You have HyperTune,
and then data labs.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.600
Those are the
tools and solutions

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:29.780
that have immediate benefit
for the autonomous ships.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:34.370
Key takeaway is basically
speed and flexibility

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.050
to bring this to
the market fast.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:41.510
So don't try to do too
many things in house.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:45.680
Partner, use open
platforms and collaboration

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.760
to drive this innovation fast.

